= The End of Anderson

Former Premier James Anderson, previously renowned for leading the Conservative Party to it's first electoral success in Grit-Dominated Saskatchewan, has formally been ousted from power. Sections of the right-wing of the CPS have always been uncomfortable with the parties growing collaboration with the Progressive Party. This culminated in a rather anti-climactic end for Anderson, forced to sign away his leadership of the party.

The Conservative Party leadership contest is set to be held six months from now. 

<div class='face-figure'>
    <img src="img/portraits/Diefenbaker_John_young.jpg" class="face-img">
</div>

The most notable figure to appear has been John Diefenbaker, a lawyer.